msgid "ROS 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros1.rst:10
#: 2ea92a7601f3416cb5b82ac15045b91e
msgid "ArduPilot capabilities can be extended with `ROS <http://www.ros.org/>`__ (aka Robot Operating System)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros1.rst:12
#: 5ba975d5d2fe4960bb80d0dccc0dc36f
msgid "`ROS <http://www.ros.org/>`__ provides libraries, tools, hardware abstraction, device drivers, visualizers, message-passing, package management, and more to help software developers create robot applications. ROS1 is being replaced by `ROS 2 <http://design.ros2.org/articles/why_ros2.html>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros1.rst:15
#: f0660fa08f1d4368b80630d40c1e9e40
msgid "If you aren't sure which version to use, the ArduPilot development team recommends ROS 2 because ROS 1 is end-of-life in 2025."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros1.rst:18
#: 08ed8b42a3b04a42aa84f7b993a068ee
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros1.rst:20
#: c38445b8cac44b2bac5714934c74fcc7
msgid "Before using ArduPilot with ROS, you should first be familiar with both ArduPilot and ROS before trying to integrate them together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros1.rst:22
#: 20cda219079e41cba452c5614f119764
msgid "Learn how to use ArduPilot first by following the relevant wiki for `Rover <https://ardupilot.org/rover/index.html>`__, `Copter <https://ardupilot.org/copter/index.html>`__ or `Plane <https://ardupilot.org/plane/index.html>`__. In particular, make sure the vehicle works well in Manual and Autonomous modes like Guided and Auto before trying to use ROS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros1.rst:23
#: e83620cb7ef24af280fe6d1a64b72062
msgid "Learn how to use ROS by reading the `ROS 1 tutorials <http://wiki.ros.org/ROS/Tutorials>`__.  In the case of a problem with ROS, it is best to ask on ROS community forums or `Robotics Stack Exchange <https://robotics.stackexchange.com/>`__ first (or google your error). You will find many other tutorials about ROS like `Emlid <https://docs.emlid.com/navio2/ros>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros1.rst:26
#: cdf6e82c2fe24af1a80947ea358c2569
msgid "MAVROS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros1.rst:28
#: 32ce3c8c01074e899f08b082272b819a
msgid "`MAVROS <http://wiki.ros.org/mavros>`__ is a ROS package that can convert between ROS topics and `MAVLink messages <https://github.com/ArduPilot/mavlink>`__ allowing ArduPilot vehicles to communicate with ROS. The `MAVROS code can be found here <https://github.com/mavlink/mavros/tree/master/mavros>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros1.rst:53
#: cf945435d735464a86b8ad8e0b38d627
msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros1.rst:55
#: b20680b9f0e1485ba12445db9e921076
msgid "ROS is capable of extending autopilot capabilities with a wider ecosystem of technologies that can run on more powerful computers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros1.rst:57
#: 1926291cebb24528b8b3cbfc58a12662
msgid "Here is ArduPilot Rover performing path planning around objects using ROS navigation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros1.rst:62
#: 3b53ea9ca03f42bc9664d359e6d98a77
msgid "We are keen to improve ArduPilot's support of ROS so if you find issues (such as commands that do not seem to be supported), please report them in the `ArduPilot issues list <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/issues>`__ with a title that includes \"ROS\" and we will attempt to resolve them as quickly as possible."
msgstr ""
